      The Academy Award for Best Original Score has been awarded at 93 consecutive ceremonies
      from 1934 to 2026, recognizing the finest achievements in film music across nine decades.
      This dataset captures every winner — one per ceremony year — along with the winning film
      and the credited composer or composers.
    </p>
    <p>
      The category has evolved considerably since its inception at the 6th Academy Awards.
      In certain years, the Academy split the award into subcategories (dramatic score versus
      comedy or musical score), but this dataset consolidates to a single winner per ceremony.
      The award has also undergone several name changes — from "Best Scoring" to "Best Original
      Score" — yet its core mission of recognizing compositional excellence in film has remained
      constant.
